  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1013 AM MST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nCurrently an upper low sits over SW OK with a ridge building in\nfrom the west. There is a back door cold front pushing through SE\nNM and will make it into far eastern areas by sunset. This isn't a\nreal strong front, but winds will pick up to 10-20mph on western\nmountain slopes. Low clouds and some patchy fog can be expected,\nespecially along the eastern slopes of the Sacs and into parts of\nHudspeth county. May see some patchy lower clouds as far west as\nEl Paso. The easterly winds will push through the remainder of the\narea overnight and start to increase out on the Lordsburg Playa by\nmorning. Tomorrow will see cooler temperatures by 5-10 degrees\neast and similar to today than out west. Did lower NBM temps out\neast where it typically has a warm bias behind these fronts and\nwith some lingering lower clouds possible. \n\nGoing into Monday night and Tuesday, there will be an upper trough\nmoving into CA and increasing southwest flow aloft. The low level\nwinds will gradually turn more southerly and tap some moisture,\nbut as the trough lifts northeast into Tue night and early Wed,\nthe best lift will remain north of the CWA, but do expect some\nlight rain showers in the Gila region and maybe some spill over\ninto the Sacs. The warm SW flow aloft will keep precip type all\nrain except some of the highest peaks. NBM may be a little high\nwith PoPs in the far NW CWA with 60s, but think sometime Tue night\nthere will be a few hundredths most areas.  \n\nWest-southwest flow continues into next weekend with temperatures\nwarming up to about 5-10 degrees above normal through Thu then a\nweak Pacific cold front moves through Fri into Sat. May bet a\nlittle breezy Fri but looks like best lift again remains north and\nlittle to no precip chances.",
